  "worked_solution": "To graph the first inequality $y<2,$ we draw the corresponding straight line $y=2.$\n\n- Since we have a strict inequality, the line itself is *not* included in the solution, so the line is dashed.\n\n- The inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *less than* those on the line, so we shade *below* the line.\n\nTo graph the second inequality $y\\ge -2,$ we draw the corresponding straight line $y=-2.$\n\n- Since we have a \"or equal to\" inequality, the line itself is included in the solution, so the line is solid.\n\n- The inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *greater than* or equal to those on the line, so we shade *above* the line.\n\nThe intersection of the solutions is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/e949882745de4727e3f611b8f958b64ed6fc08c0097508970501a16f68374cf2.png)",
